## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a scalable, multilingual vector-search pipeline with practical constraints like latency, freshness, and safety.

## Key Concepts
- Retrieval-augmented generation with embeddings
- Semantic chunking with overlap and size bounds
- Vector DB selection (HNSW, indexing, sharding)
- Cross-encoder reranking for result quality
- Update pipelines and data freshness guards

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: indexing
function indexDocs(docs){
  for (const d of docs){
    const chunks = chunk(d.text, 800, 100); // size, overlap
    for (const c of chunks){
      const embedding = embed(c);
      await vectorDB.store(embedding, c);
    }
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Understanding cross-language adapter strategies with strict latency and memory constraints.

## Key Concepts
- PEFT vs full fine-tuning in multi-language QA
- Adapter injection points (attention vs MLP)
- Language tagging vs per-language adapters
- Latency/memory budgeting and rollback plans

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo adapter injection sketch
function attachAdapters(model, keys) {
  for (const m of model.modules()) {
    if (m instanceof AttentionLayer || m instanceof MLP) {
      m.addAdapter({rank: 8, name: keys.next()});
    }
  }
  return model;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you monitor drift between languages post-deployment?
- What failure modes require bypassing adapters and using base model instead?

## Why Asked
